```
Reason: `ns_name` is set to point to `ent->ns_name`, but `ent->ns_name` is not set to NULL. Later, `aa_load_ent_free(ent)` frees `ent->ns_name`, and then `kfree(ns_name)` attempts to free the same memory again, causing a double free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
ns_name = ent->ns_name;
ent->ns_name = NULL;
```
Reason: After transferring ownership of the string to `ns_name`, setting `ent->ns_name` to NULL prevents `aa_load_ent_free(ent)` from freeing it, thus avoiding the double free when `kfree(ns_name)` is called later.

